----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Credits and third-party components
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

libimobiledevice — https://libimobiledevice.org  (LGPL-2.1-or-later / GPL-2.0+)
    The cross-platform library and tools (ideviceinfo, idevicepair,
    idevicebackup2, ifuse via libimobiledevice/AFC, …) that do all the real
    device communication. iPhone Link invokes these as external programs and
    streams their output; it does not include or modify their source.

UxPlay by FDH2 — https://github.com/FDH2/UxPlay  (GPL-3.0)
    The AirPlay mirroring/audio receiver used by the Media page so the iPhone can
    stream its screen and audio to this PC. iPhone Link runs `uxplay` as an
    external program; it does not include or modify its source. UxPlay is an
    optional dependency — without it, only the AirPlay receiver is unavailable.

ifuse — https://github.com/libimobiledevice/ifuse  (LGPL-2.1-or-later)
    FUSE mount of the device's media (DCIM) and per-app File-Sharing folders,
    used by the Photos, Documents and Media pages. Invoked as an external program.

GStreamer — https://gstreamer.freedesktop.org  (LGPL-2.1)
    `gst-play-1.0` plays a selected camera-roll video locally, and GStreamer is
    UxPlay's rendering backend. Invoked as external programs.

Arch Linux Tweak Tool (ATT) by Erik Dubois — https://www.arcolinux.com  (GPL-3.0)
    The look and feel of the GTK4 interface, the in-app toast notification, and
    several CSS values are modelled on ATT (by way of the sibling Disk Recovery
    Tool). With thanks to Erik Dubois and the ArcoLinux community.

iDescriptor — https://github.com/iDescriptor/iDescriptor  (AGPL-3.0)
    Consulted as a design REFERENCE only (notably that UxPlay is the practical
    way to receive AirPlay on Linux). No iDescriptor source is included or copied;
    iPhone Link remains GPL-3.0.

Apple Notes / Messages on-device formats
    The Notes and Messages exporters parse the device's own SQLite databases
    (NoteStore.sqlite, sms.db) from an unencrypted backup, including the gzip/zlib
    protobuf note bodies and the typedstream attributedBody message text. This is
    original parsing code; the database formats are Apple's.

GTK 4 / PyGObject
    The graphical toolkit and Python bindings.
